    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi José,<div><br></div><div>Actually, there is nothing wrong. All that happened is that your code failed to initialize, and in this case that manifested itself with an error reported from R.  However the model-building then proceeded and finished.</div><div><br></div><div>You can use &quot;calculate = FALSE&quot; to avoid having nimbleModel try to initialize (including calculations) the entire model, which will avoid the error message (and often run faster).</div><div><br></div><div>Perry</div><div><br><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Mon, Jan 29, 2018 at 11:21 AM, Jose Jimenez <span dir=\"ltr\">&lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">Jose.J...@uclm.es</a>&gt;</span> wrote:<br></div></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
