    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div lang=\"ES\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><div><div><div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi José,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Actually, there is nothing wrong. All that happened is that your code failed to initialize, and in this case that manifested itself with an error reported from R.  However the model-building then proceeded and finished.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">You can use &quot;calculate = FALSE&quot; to avoid having nimbleModel try to initialize (including calculations) the entire model, which will avoid the error message (and often run faster).<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Perry<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></div></div></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
